### Auth Controller Tests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiBase = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth
@userId = a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a5b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d

### Register a new user
POST {{apiBase}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser@example.com",
  "username": "newuser123",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "first_name": "John",
  "last_name": "Doe",
  "bio": "Hello, I'm a new user!"
}

### Login with credentials (save token for later)
# @name login
POST {{apiBase}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john_doe",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Extract token from login response
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Get current user profile (requires auth)
GET {{apiBase}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update current user profile (requires auth)
PUT {{apiBase}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Johnny",
  "last_name": "Doe",
  "bio": "Updated bio information"
}

### Get specific user by ID (public)
GET {{apiBase}}/users/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### Logout (requires auth)
DELETE {{apiBase}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Test: Try to access protected route without token (should fail)
GET {{apiBase}}/me
